 "summary": "Neither Mathlib nor Tau Ceti already has the general-genus `weierstrassFactor`, the negated-`logTaylor` sum and derivative lemmas in `Complex/Log/Taylor.lean`, or the sharp radial bound: the Mathlib grep finds no Weierstrass-factor material outside power-series preparation, and the only `logTaylor (p + 1) (-z)` hits in Tau Ceti are this PR's own. The PR deletes `weierstrassFactorOne` and the repeated `logTaylor` induction in `Log/Bounds.lean`, and its proofs reuse Mathlib's `hasDerivAt_logTaylor`, `mul_neg_geom_sum`, `intervalIntegral.integral_unitInterval_deriv_eq_sub` and `intervalIntegral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le`.",
